Subject: [PATCH] =?UTF-8?q?=E2=9C=A8=20Add=20Scaleway=20and=20UpCloud=20cl?=
 =?UTF-8?q?oud=20providers?=
MIME-Version: 1.0
Content-Type: text/plain; charset=UTF-8
Content-Transfer-Encoding: 8bit

Expand Infra > Cloud providers with two more single-credential
REST providers, following the existing client pattern (shared
OkHttp client, org.json parsing, Dispatchers.IO, CloudAuthException
only on 401/403).

- ScalewayClient: X-Auth-Token auth against the zoned Instance API.
  Iterates all public zones, paginates until a short page, and
  treats a 404 zone as empty rather than an error. Power actions
  probe zones until one accepts. powercycle maps to force restart.
- UpCloudClient: HTTP Basic auth with the credential packed as
  api_username:api_password (same convention as AWS's
  AKID:SECRET:REGION). GET /1.3/server returns every server with
  inline ip_addresses, so no per-server detail call is needed.
  Start/stop/restart use the documented stop_server / restart_server
  bodies; force restart is a hard restart with timeout_action destroy.
- CloudProviderType: adds SCALEWAY and UPCLOUD entries with token
  help, and wires both into newClient(). The add-account provider
  spinner and registry resolve providers from the enum, so the
  new entries appear with the correct credential hint and no
  other call site needed changes.
